# Nick Giblin

LSV's State Emergency Management Officer. Key stakeholder on the LIMSOC 2026-27 SME-group process: nominated as channel for the SDO, SAC and ARO representatives across three of the four SME groups (Incident Categorisation and Flow, Call Out Systems and Capabilities, AI within Incident Management Practice). His engagement is load-bearing for the EOI to ship.

## Working relationship

Has not been returning calls (as at 2026-06-09). Engagement model has shifted to written email instead of further phone attempts. Alex Walton has directed Nick to go via the area leads rather than broadcasting nominations.

## Facts

- Spelt **Giblin**, not "Gilblin" — easy to mistype.
- Two distinct "Nick"s in the LIMSOC thread: Nick Giblin (SEMO) and Nick W (LSV Comms / SLCO, this principal).
- Reviewer-side of the SME EOI process; not a decision-maker on whether projects proceed.

## Live commitments

- Confirm framing of the SME approach (target by Friday 12 June 2026).
- Nominate SDO / SAC / ARO reps for the three groups he leads channel on.

## Acronyms in his orbit

- SDO = State Duty Officer
- SAC = State Agency Commander
- ARO = Area Response Officer
- SEMO = State Emergency Management Officer
